<section class="hero">
  <h1>bitmark and JSON editors, for any web app</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Monaco editors for bitmark, with the JSON, HTML, XML, Text, Info and Mappings views beside them. Edit any pane
    and the others follow, through the bitmark parser. Use them from plain JavaScript, a static page, React or
    Angular.
  </p>
  <div class="buttons">
    <a class="button button-primary" href="/getting-started/">Get started</a>
    <a class="button" href="/demos/try-it/">Try the full editor</a>
    <a class="button" href="/api/">API reference</a>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="demo">
  <div class="demo-bar">
    <span>Edit either side: the other one follows.</span>
    <span>bitmark ⇄ JSON</span>
  </div>
  <bitmark-session class="demo-stage" lazy="idle" narrow="static" theme="auto" value="[.article]
Hello **World**!

[.cloze]
The capital of France is [_Paris].">
    <pre data-bitmark-static><code>[.article]
Hello **World**!

[.cloze]
The capital of France is [_Paris].</code></pre>
    <div class="demo-panes">
      <bitmark-pane type="bitmark" label="bitmark"></bitmark-pane>
      <bitmark-pane type="json" label="JSON"></bitmark-pane>
    </div>
  </bitmark-session>
</div>

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Panes you place anywhere</h3>
    <p>One document per session, shown in any number of panes: bitmark, JSON, HTML, XML, Text, Info and Mappings.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Any framework</h3>
    <p>A plain TypeScript core, custom elements, a React adapter and Angular components.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Your Monaco, or ours</h3>
    <p>Pass the Monaco your app already has, or load <code>/bundled</code>, which brings its own.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>The real parser</h3>
    <p>Highlighting, errors, completion and hover come from <code>@gmb/bitmark-parser</code>, injected or loaded.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="prose">
  <h2>Install</h2>
  <p>With a bundler (React, Angular, Vite, webpack…):</p>
{% highlight "sh" %}
npm install @gmb/bitmark-editor monaco-editor
{% endhighlight %}
  <p>On a static page, from the CDN:</p>
{% highlight "html" %}
<script type="module" src="{{ site.cdn }}"></script>
{% endhighlight %}
  <p>
    Then pick your setup in <a href="/getting-started/">Getting started</a>, or open a
    <a href="/demos/example-apps/">complete example app</a>.
  </p>
</div>

